  "body": "## What (plan \u00a73 \u2014 the MVP demo)\n- `src/live.rs`: `LiveSource` implements the TUI's `Source` over real data: `agents::discover` \u2192 Agents rows (state, `waiting_for`, age from the registry or `/proc/<pid>/stat`, cwd, branch, title, last prompt, raw detail JSON); `Board` \u2192 active claims and the last 50 entries; `load` from `/proc/loadavg`; the `~/.bf/AGENT_CHAT.md` digest is regenerated with a **Live agents** section on the first snapshot, every 30 s while the screen runs, and after any stop/note/expire. `stop` \u2192 `runner::stop` + a board `stop` entry as the operator; `note` \u2192 addressed board note; `expire_claim` \u2192 release \"expired by operator\".\n- `src/runner.rs`: `stop(pid)`: refuses pid \u2264 1, anything in bf's own ancestry, and bf's own process group; pgid from `/proc/<pid>/stat` field 5 (never assumed = pid); `/bin/kill -TERM -- -pgid`, poll \u2264 5 s, then `-KILL` \u2264 2 s; zombies count as gone. Unit tests for the stat parser and the guards.\n- `src/main.rs`: bare `bf` \u2192 `tui::run(LiveSource)`; `bf stop <pid>` \u2192 human-only guard (`identity::current`), then stop + record. Nothing else changed.\n- `tests/cli_wiring.rs`: bare `bf` without a tty prints `AGENTS (0)` / `CLAIMS (0)` under empty fixture dirs, then `CLAIMS (1)` with `c-1` after a claim; `bf stop 1` \u2192 exit 2; `bf stop <own-group sleep>` \u2192 exit 0 \"after TERM\", the process is gone and `bf board --all` shows the `stop` entry (the test pins `BF_PROC` to a tree containing only the target so the guard is deterministic under any shell).\n- `tests/cli_skeleton.rs`: `stop` leaves the exit-3 list; the bare-`bf` test pins `BF_DATA_DIR`/`BF_HOME`/`BF_PROC` so it does not read this host's real sessions.\n\n## Evidence on this host (2026-09-18 16:58Z, load ~60)\n`bf </dev/null` \u2192 exit 0, **33 agents** (claude 7, codex 17, grok 7, cursor 2), busy/idle/waiting states, titles from the registries (e.g. `claude 3085429 busy 2h /home/ubuntu/bullet bulletfarm-lean-tui-launch`). `BF_TUI_ONCE=1 bf` renders `bf \u00b7 agents 33 (claude 7 codex 17 grok 7 cursor 2) \u00b7 busy 1 \u00b7 claims 0 \u00b7 PRs 0` with the Agents and Detail panes. Local: fmt/clippy `-D warnings` clean; 43 tests (lib 20, cli_agents 2, cli_board 2, cli_skeleton 5, cli_wiring 3, core 3, tui 8); `bash scripts/check` EXIT 0 in 16 s.\n\nKnown follow-ups (not in this PR): the Codex count includes wrapper processes (dedupe by session \u2014 discovery follow-up #2); transcript tail is empty until discovery exposes a tail helper; `--data-dir` is ignored by the board/live paths (they read `BF_DATA_DIR`/`HOME`).\n\n## Review\nReviewer must be a different vendor (grok, codex or cursor): `REVIEW: approve <head-sha>` via `gh pr review --comment`, then `gh pr merge --rebase --delete-branch`.\n\nbf-author: claude/claude-orch \u00b7 bf-claim: AGENT_CHAT.md 2026-09-18T16:53Z\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
